      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. this is good but maybe a bit too stiff? can you give me a version that feels a little more \"human\" and warm, maybe emphasizing that it was a really tough call for the team? like, something that feels less like a form letter and more like it's coming from a real person who actually liked them.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Absolutely, here's a more personal and warm version:\n\n---\n\nSubject: Thanks for Consideration – We Miss Your Energy – [Applicant's Name]\n\nHi [Applicant's Name],\n\nI hope you're doing well. I wanted to take a moment to personally thank you for chatting with us and sharing your journey during the hiring process. It really means a lot knowing we had the chance to learn from your passion and drive – qualities that we're always excited to see.\n\nIt was incredibly tough for our team to make the final decision, especially since you stood out so much. We appreciated the time and energy you invested in such a meaningful conversation, and we're sorry to say that we've decided to go with someone whose specific skill set aligns a bit more closely with what we're looking for right now.\n\nYour enthusiasm was infectious, and the thoughtfulness you brought to your career discussion truly inspired us. However, as much as we'd love to have you on board with [Company Name], we've moved in a slightly different direction. \n\nPlease know that our door remains open for the future, and we'd be more than willing to revisit your application should another opportunity arise that fits a good match.\n\nThank you again for your hard work, and we wish you all the best on your journey moving forward.",
